REPLACE_THIS_ENTIRE_FILE_WITH_A_RANDOM_PASSWORD

# ==============================================================================
# Ansible Vault password file
# ==============================================================================
# Copy to .vault_pass (gitignored), replacing the contents with a strong random
# value and NOTHING else — no comments, no trailing blank lines. Ansible reads
# the whole file as the password.
#
#     openssl rand -base64 32 > .vault_pass
#     chmod 600 .vault_pass
#
# ansible.cfg points at this path, so ansible-playbook decrypts group_vars/all/
# vault.yml automatically.
#
# Store the real password in a password manager. Lose it and the vault is
# unrecoverable — Vault uses AES-256 with no backdoor and no reset.
# ==============================================================================
